Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||08-31-2001||12:58 PM||||I don't know how many of you out there read GRM , but for the last 3 (2?) years they have held a challenge. Build a car within a budget constraint and race it against others.<P><BR>Over on the Fiero racing list we are plotting to build such a beast. Were lead by George Ryan , some of you may know him as having built likley the fastest autocross Fiero in north America..1900lbs , quad 4 230hp.<P>Well George is now planning to build a car for the challenge, with the help of a lot of people (Ed parks , doug chase , all sorts of well knowns). The car is going to be an 88 with a 4.9ltr caddy motor. it will be gutted to probably the 2000lbs range with the motor.<P>I believe the event is next feburary in Flordia , I will be flying down to take part.<P>Were looking for various parts / performance / otherwise cheap. I have already offered to give my NOS setup for the dragstrip part of the challenge. This should yield a mid 12 sec car.<P>If you can give a hand in the building of this email george @<P>gryan3@mindspring.com <P>Would be nice to see a Fiero Take a top position and get some coverage in a national magazine. As racers we have kind of been misplaced by the SCCA and put into classes where we can't be competitive. George has already lined up a national Champ to drive the car in the autocross portion of the event , so our chances are good!.<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||08-31-2001||01:08 PM||||Keep us updated... and include a shopping list of what you might be looking for.  We can certainly pool together some resources!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||08-31-2001||02:03 PM||||I believe Bob Parker (Kick Hill) is whipping up a car for that thing also- 3.4 DOHC||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||08-31-2001||02:05 PM||||I am sure you and George know 1000 times more about autoX then I do, but, would the 4.9 motor be the best?  I would think a HO Quad 4 would be a better choice.  4.9 Caddy motor doesn't strike me as much of an AutoXer.  Is it just AutoX that they compete in?  <P>Anyway, sounds cool if it all works out.  I would love to see a Fiero in a nat'l magazine.||||reg||14
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||08-31-2001||03:23 PM||||George spent thousands building his quad 4 car. The motor was professionally built and dynoed 232Hp.  One of the events is a drag racing. Georges quad 4 car @ 1900 lbs turned a low 13 in the 1/4 , I think the draw to the caddy motor is dollar per HP and ease of install.<P>Nothing beats low end grunt. Come off of  a tight corner with a quad 4 and your caught without torque. The torque curve on a 4.9 is vast. while it doesn't rev too high , the low end torque is a good trade off, espically for the drag race portion.<P>JM <P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
